\section*{1. Thermodynamic Power Envelope}

The Sovereign Matter Engine operates at a continuous power scale
\[
P_0 = 1.0 \times 10^{16}\,\text{W}
\]
corresponding to a 10-petawatt relativistic matter-to-energy conversion regime.

\section*{2. Matter-to-Energy Conversion}

Let \(c\) denote the speed of light and \(\eta \in (0,1]\) the conversion efficiency.

\subsection*{2.1 General Relation}

The required matter conversion rate is
\[
\frac{dm}{dt} = \frac{P}{\eta c^2}.
\]

\subsection*{2.2 Ideal Efficiency}

For \(\eta = 1\),
\[
\left.\frac{dm}{dt}\right|_{\eta=1} = \frac{10^{16}}{c^2}.
\]

\subsection*{2.3 Engineering Efficiency}

For \(\eta = 0.95\),
\[
\left.\frac{dm}{dt}\right|_{\eta=0.95} = \frac{10^{16}}{0.95\,c^2}.
\]

\section*{3. Relativistic Field Description}

The core matter engine is modeled via the relativistic stress-energy tensor
\[
T^{\mu\nu} = (\rho_m + p)u^\mu u^\nu + p\,g^{\mu\nu} + S^{\mu\nu}_{\text{radiation}},
\]
where:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \(\rho_m\) is the matter density field,
    \item \(p\) is isotropic pressure,
    \item \(u^\mu\) is the four-velocity,
    \item \(g^{\mu\nu}\) is the spacetime metric,
    \item \(S^{\mu\nu}_{\text{radiation}}\) encodes directional radiative flux at petawatt scales.
\end{itemize}

The dynamics obey the conservation law
\[
\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu} = 0.
\]

\section*{4. Mass-Energy Balance}

Over a simulation interval \(\Delta t\), the generated energy is
\[
E_{\text{gen}} = P_0 \Delta t,
\]
and the corresponding consumed mass is
\[
m_{\text{consumed}} = \frac{E_{\text{gen}}}{\eta c^2}.
\]

Consistency requires
\[
E_{\text{gen}} = m_{\text{consumed}} c^2
\]
within numerical tolerance.

\section*{5. Causality Constraint}

The four-velocity satisfies
\[
u^\mu u_\mu = -c^2,
\]
and physical states must obey
\[
\lVert \vec{v} \rVert \le c,
\]
ensuring relativistic causality in all fluid and field updates.

\section*{6. Radiative \& Thermal Balance}

Let \(Q_{\text{rad}}\) denote radiative losses and \(Q_{\text{th}}\) thermal waste.  
For a steady-state 10-PW engine,
\[
P_0 = P_{\text{useful}} + Q_{\text{rad}} + Q_{\text{th}},
\]
with subsystem consumption and cooling fields constrained such that
\[
P_{\text{useful}} \le P_0,\quad Q_{\text{rad}}, Q_{\text{th}} \ge 0.
\]

